# Line endings are not cosmetic here. The packs are stored LF and CI checks them
# out that way, but a Windows working copy gets CRLF via core.autocrlf, and any
# pack a user writes in Notepad is CRLF too. The macOS parser used to trim only
# spaces, so each message kept a trailing carriage return and a blank line became
# an empty speech bubble. The parser handles both now; this keeps the repo's own
# files from drifting into the same shape.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Message packs are read line by line by both apps: keep them LF everywhere.
*.txt text eol=lf

# PowerShell is happier with CRLF, and these are only ever run on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.dmg binary
*.zip binary
